      <h2>Emergency Plumber Liverpool. Common Questions</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to the questions Liverpool folk ask most.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">MINIMUM CHARGE</span>&nbsp; Is there a minimum charge?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We charge a minimum of 1 hour on all call-outs. Weekdays 9am to 5pm that is £80. Weekends 9am to 1pm that is £120. Out of hours that is £150. After the first hour we charge in 30 minute blocks. Parts are charged at cost. A written quote is given before any work begins beyond the first diagnosis.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Fixed hourly rates with a 1 hour minimum. Weekdays 9am to 5pm £80. Weekends 9am to 1pm £120. Out of hours nights and bank holidays £150. After the first hour we charge in 30 minute blocks. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost between £80 and £350. Written quote before work begins.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All our team are Gas Safe. Working on gas without it is against the law. Check us at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We give a gas cert for every gas job.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">ENGINEERS</span>&nbsp; Do you use sub-contractors?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>No. Every engineer we send is on our engineers. We never use subbies. We never use agency workers. You get the same trained, vetted, insured team each time.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach me in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We aim to be there in 30 minutes. We cover all of Liverpool L1 to L40. Inner Liverpool is often under 20 mins. The outer ring takes about 35.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">POSTCODES</span>&nbsp; What postcodes do you cover in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We cover all 40 Liverpool postcodes. That is L1 right through to L40. See the area links above to find your postcode.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COMMERCIAL</span>&nbsp; Do you cover commercial properties in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We do 24/7 emergency plumbing for Liverpool businesses. Shops, cafes, offices, hotels, warehouses. Same fixed rates as homes. No business top-up. We can invoice on 30-day terms for set-up firms.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All our work carries a full 12-month workmanship guarantee. If anything we fix fails within 12 months due to our work we come back and sort it at no charge. No argument. No quibble.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">FROZEN PIPES</span>&nbsp; What should I do if my pipes are frozen in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Do not try to thaw frozen pipes with a naked flame. Turn off the water at the stopcock at once. Call us at once. A frozen pipe costs far less to fix than a burst one. Liverpool's Victorian terraces are very at risk due to external and loft pipes that were never lagged to modern standards.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">INSURANCE</span>&nbsp; Can you help with water damage insurance claims?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We provide full docs for insurance claims. An itemised invoice. Photos of the damage and repair. A written report on the cause. Gas safety certificates where needed. We can also speak to your insurer directly if needed.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LANDLORDS</span>&nbsp; Do you work with Liverpool landlords and letting agents?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We work with landlords and letting agents in Liverpool, Wirral and St Helens. CP12 gas certs from £80. We handle tenant call-outs. We offer cover plans for landlords with a few rentals. See <a href="https://www.nrla.org.uk/resources/looking-after-your-property/landlords-gas-safety-responsibilities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NRLA landlord gas safety guidance</a> for the legal duties.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">3AM</span>&nbsp; Do you really answer calls at 3am?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. A real person answers 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. No voicemail. No automated system. No call centre. We answer within 3 rings. Christmas Day. Bank Holidays. 3am Sunday mornings. Call us right now to test it.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">NO HOT WATER</span>&nbsp; What should I do if I have no hot water in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Check your boiler pressure gauge first. It should read between 1 and 1.5 bar. Below 0.5 bar, repressurise using the filling loop. Note any error codes on the boiler display before calling us. If neither fixes the issue, call us on 0151 558 0334. We attend no hot water emergencies 24/7 across Liverpool.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BLOCKED DRAIN</span>&nbsp; What should I do if my toilet is blocked or overflowing?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Stop flushing at once. More flushing will overflow sewage onto the floor. Turn off the water supply to the toilet at the isolation valve on the pipe behind it if you can. Call us on 0151 558 0334. Do not use chemical drain cleaners. They rarely work on full blockages and can damage older Liverpool pipework.</p></div></details>
